{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "modelVersion": "memory-select-v2",
  "description": "How Michael chooses which saved memories to read for a question. The Next.js server loads the caller's own memories (one user's, or one organization's, filtered in SQL by scope, expiry and sensitivity) and sends at most maxItems of them, each under a request-local ref and without any id. services/intelligence/app/memory/selection.py ranks them deterministically by overlap with the question — of words, of related-word groups (\"like\" and \"prefer\", \"evening\" and \"tonight\") and of the part of day a clock time falls in (\"8pm\" is evening) — rarer terms counting more, newer memories first on a tie, and returns at most `limit` refs. With no question, or when nothing overlaps, it returns the newest. No model is called, and semantic retrieval is deferred until this is measured as insufficient.",
